WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.1 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
From work to structure

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Structure follows the work: list the functions your strategy needs before naming any roles.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
A function is a body of work your strategy needs, such as delivery, finance or communications. It is not a person: at the start, one founder may hold several functions.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
Three ways to resource it

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:38.981
In-house: You or a co-founder do the work yourselves, with your own time and skills. For example: One founder of a repair café runs the sessions and recruits the volunteer fixers.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:49.570
Shared with a partner: A partner does part of the work alongside you, under an agreement. For example: A library hosts the tutoring service and promotes it to local families.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:01:02.100
Contracted out: You pay someone for a defined task, but a founder still checks the work. For example: A bookkeeper keeps the bakery's accounts; a founder reviews them every month.

8
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.100
Why start from functions

9
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.774
1. You see all the work, including what nobody has started yet.

10
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:14.448
2. You spot where one founder carries too much, before a crisis.

11
00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:21.493
3. You know what your first volunteers, hires or partners should take on.

12
00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:22.493
What they guide

13
00:01:22.493 --> 00:01:27.426
1. Your organigram: functions become your first roles and lines.

14
00:01:27.426 --> 00:01:32.359
2. Your role cards: each function gets one accountable owner.

15
00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:39.033
3. Your workforce plan and budget: what to fill first, and how.

16
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:40.033
What to avoid

17
00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:45.707
Starting from the people you know instead of the work needed.

18
00:01:45.707 --> 00:01:50.641
Forgetting work not yet started, like registration or bookkeeping.

19
00:01:50.641 --> 00:01:57.685
Thinking a contracted task no longer needs anyone inside to check it.

20
00:01:58.285 --> 00:02:00.085
You list your functions and how each will be resourced at the start.

21
00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:04.085
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:05.585 --> 00:02:08.685
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
